<BaseLayout title="About — Woodland Kin" description="The story behind Woodland Kin — mountain rooted apparel from Big Bear Valley, California.">
  <section class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-20">
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-10">About Woodland Kin</h1>

    <div class="aspect-[21/9] bg-theme-surface rounded-lg flex items-center justify-center mb-12">
      <span class="text-theme-muted text-sm"><!-- TODO: Replace placeholder images with real assets -->[Big Bear Valley Panorama]</span>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-theme-muted leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Woodland Kin was born in Big Bear Valley, California — a small mountain community tucked into the San Bernardino National Forest. Up here, life moves at a different pace. The air is thinner, the nights are colder, and the people are closer. We started this brand because we wanted clothing that reflected the place we call home: honest, durable, and rooted in something real.
      </p>

      <p>
        Our designs are drawn from the ridgelines, the pines, the old trails, and the families who have been walking them for generations. Every graphic is made in collaboration with local artists who know these mountains — not from stock libraries or trend reports. When you wear Woodland Kin, you're wearing a piece of Big Bear.
      </p>

      <p>
        We print on demand because we believe in making what's needed, not flooding the world with excess. Every order is produced individually, which means less waste, more intention, and a product that was made for you. Our blanks are heavyweight, pre-shrunk, and built for the kind of wear that mountain life demands.
      </p>

      <p>
        A portion of every sale goes to San Bernardino National Forest conservation efforts — because this place gave us everything, and we intend to give back. Woodland Kin isn't a lifestyle brand. It's a community. Welcome to the kin.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
